 of years. In this book, Dale Greenwalt introduces readers to the new science of ancient biomolecules and what it tells about the lives of long extinct life. Ancient biomolecules, as we learn, give us a whole new view into the past. After an introductory explanation of what biomolecules are (and are not), each chapter treats an ancient biomolecule and what it can teach us about a long-dead organism and how it may have lived.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-remnants-of-ancient-life-the-new-science-of-old-fossils-dale-greenwalt.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0.356,"traits":[{"id":"academic","score":0.38,"confidence":"low","evidence":["academic press signal: Princeton University Press / Princeton University Press"]},{"id":"scholarly","score":0.28,"confidence":"low","evidence":["academic press signal: Princeton University Press / Princeton University Press"]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"New technologies let scientists recover ancient biomolecules from fossils, enabling interpretations of extinct organisms that revise prior rock-only views of the fossil record.","confidence":0.74},"academicOrientation":{"score":65,"confidence":0.46},"profileConfidence":0.72,"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"5b158221fff870d8584cba962e0062422af0cdcbbaa5f0809a333870d7c7240a","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Science","secondarySubjects":["Nature & Environment"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book focuses on the new scientific insights into ancient biomolecules derived from fossils, making Science the dominant subject, while it also engages with themes of natural history, justifying the inclusion of Nature & Environment as a secondary subject.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inpu